     9	Marks: worth (worth / trivia / duplicate); answer (supported / unsupported / insufficient), not asked on a card with no answer. A mark still
    10	split after two rounds is {"split": [codex mark, claude mark]}. A debate round reads only the rounds before it and resends the whole brief
    11	(closed sessions remember nothing); a round is complete only when every mark it owes is written (`round-N.done`), and readings refuse a deck
    12	whose three rounds are not complete. The guardrail sample draws from the system's own ids (`source_id`), sorted as strings (verdict-rule.json).
    13	A field both families agree on in a round stays settled; later rounds change only fields still disputed. A plant moves the stored rung one
    14	place and enters the deck only when a separate closed reader confirms the moved answer is not supported (as supported controls are confirmed
    15	supported first). A card's covering mark is true, "split" (resolved per counting by the scorer) or false. The deck never overwrites a key.
